          "type": "Block",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": "---\nesid: sec-partitiondatetimepattern\ndescription: >\n  Temporal dates outside the TimeClip range are correctly formatted when the\n  locale uses non-Latin numerals (e.g., Arabic-Indic digits).\ninfo: |\n  When a Temporal plain object is outside the range representable by a legacy\n  Date and the locale's numbering system uses non-Latin digits, the\n  implementation must re-format the adjusted day value in the correct numeral\n  system.\nfeatures: [Temporal]\nlocale: [ar-EG]\n---"
        },
        {
          "type": "Line",
          "position": "before",
          "sameLine": false,
          "value": " Arabic-Egyptian locale uses Arabic-Indic digits (U+0660..U+0669)"
        }
      ]
